---
import Shell from '../../../../../../src/layouts/Shell.astro';
import Brand from '../../../../../../src/components/Brand.astro';
import '../../../../../styles.css';
---
<Shell title="MVP preview privacy · Koverr" description="How the Koverr preview uses data." noindex referrerPolicy="no-referrer">
  <div class="check-app">
    <header class="check-header">
      <div class="wrap check-header-inner"><Brand /><a class="check-link" href="/">Back to preview</a></div>
    </header>
    <main id="main" class="wrap check-main">
      <article class="check-privacy check-intro">
        <h1>Preview privacy</h1>
        <p>The leak check uses fictional results. Fix progress and any skip reasons stay in the current browser tab. Select Exit sample to clear them.</p>
        <h2>Password check</h2>
        <p>Your browser sends only the first five characters of a hash to <a href="https://haveibeenpwned.com/Passwords">Pwned Passwords</a>. It matches the returned candidates locally and clears the input. Koverr receives neither the password nor its hash and does not store the result.</p>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</Shell>
